%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
That was what I kept telling myself. Yet tonight... I\nended up putting my problematic superior above her, even\nif for a short time.%K%P
话虽然这么说，\n但我还要照顾身边这个让人焦头烂额的上司。%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dIs she there with you?  Is she sleeping there in the same\nroom with you?\d%K%P
「姫绪姐在那里吗？\n在理君的身边，睡着了吗？」%K%P
Mitoko, who had recently been robbed of the love of her\nparents, could intuitively sense the doubt that crept into\nmy heart.%K%P
最近刚刚失去了亲情的美都子，\n一定能敏感地察觉到我内心的动摇吧。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...We're not together. I'm outside the hotel right now.\d%K%P
「…她不在我身边啊。\n我现在在宾馆的外边」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dWhy? Weren't you looking after her?\d%K%P
「为什么？\n这么离开真的好吗？」%K%P
She cared more about the woman who made me worry by\ndrinking herself to the ground than the mischievous child\nthat made me worry with her sudden disappearance.%K%P
即便如此，比起那个过了门限时间不回家的熊孩子，\n这个不胜酒力的坏女人，更让我担心。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dYou don't have to worry; she woke up just a short while\nago. There's no need for me to be there and babysit her\nall the time.\d%K%P
「她刚才醒了，已经没事儿了。\n即使我不在…也会没问题吧」%K%P
%LCMitoko
%LC美都子
\dReally...?\d%K%P
「真的、吗？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dYeah. With that said, I'm on my way home right now.\d%K%P
「嗯，是的。\n所以现在，我要回去了」%K%P
It was not too late yet.%K%P
即便是现在也不迟。%K%P
All I had to do was check out, catch a taxi, and see\nMitoko's face -- that would surely dispel all my doubts.%K%P
退房，打个出租车，\n看见美都子，我就能安心下来。%K%P
